    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\"><span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span><span class=\"time\">15 min</span><span class=\"chip ok\">Easy</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Hashing</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Sliding window</span><a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/contains-duplicate-ii/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 219</a></div>\n  <h1>Contains Duplicate II</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Insight in one line: an index can only pair with the k indices just before it, so keep exactly those k values in a hash set and slide it; a hit on insert is the answer. O(n) time, O(min(n, k)) space. The equally good one-liner idea: remember the latest index of every value.</p>\n"
  },
